# 14. Count-Focused Fine-Tuning

After selecting the best multitask checkpoint, the notebook performs a separate **count-focused fine-tuning stage**.

The motivation in the notebook is to improve count prediction without substantially disturbing the learned classification representation.

The procedure is:

```text
Best multitask checkpoint
          ↓
      Load model
          ↓
Filter batches to count questions
          ↓
Use count regression loss only
          ↓
Learning rate = 5e-6
          ↓
Fine-tune
          ↓
Save final count-finetuned model
```

The fine-tuning optimizer is:

```python
AdamW(
    model.parameters(),
    lr=5e-6,
    weight_decay=1e-4
)
```

The count objective remains:

```python
MSELoss(
    predicted_log_count,
    log1p(actual_count)
)
```

The resulting model is saved as:

```text
best_count_finetuned_rsvqa.pt
```

The notebook reports a model size of approximately:

```text
753.88 MB
```

A compressed ZIP version was approximately:

```text
698.69 MB
```

The notebook also split the model into eight 100 MB parts for easier file handling.

