# 26. Summary

This project implements a **multimodal multitask RSVQA model** that combines:

```text
ViT
+
BERT
+
MLP Fusion
+
Multiple Task Heads
```

The model receives both the satellite image and natural-language question and jointly supports:

```text
Presence classification
Composition/comparison classification
Rural/urban classification
Count regression
```

The final experimental pipeline consists of:

```text
RSVQA-LR
   ↓
Image preprocessing with ViTImageProcessor
   ↓
Question tokenization with BERT tokenizer
   ↓
ViT image encoder
   +
BERT text encoder
   ↓
1536-D concatenated representation
   ↓
768 → 512 fusion network
   ↓
Four task-specific prediction heads
   ↓
Multitask training
   ↓
Best checkpoint selection
   ↓
Count-focused fine-tuning
   ↓
Official test evaluation
```

The final official test evaluation reported:

```text
Presence accuracy     : 90.80%
Composition accuracy  : 91.95%
Rural/Urban accuracy  : 88.00%

Count MAE              : 63.74
Count RMSE             : 265.85
Count Exact            : 22.09%
Count ±1               : 35.46%
Count ±5               : 53.82%
Count ±10              : 62.06%
```

This repository provides the implementation and experimental workflow for building and evaluating the SatQuery-RSVQA multimodal model.
